      "math_academy_id": "e-5135",
      "problem": "What is the result of dividing $\\dfrac 3 x$ by $\\dfrac y {6x^2}?$",
      "worked_solution": "To compute\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{3}{x} \\div \\dfrac{y}{6x^2},\n$$\n\nwe just need to multiply by the reciprocal of the divisor:\n\n$$\n\\require{cancel}\n\t\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\dfrac 3 x \\div  \\dfrac y {6x^2} &=\\\n\t\t\\dfrac 3 x \\cdot  \\dfrac {6x^2} y &=\\\n\t\t\\dfrac {18x^2} {xy}&=\\\n\t\t\\dfrac {18x^\\cancel{2}} {\\cancel{x}y}&=\\\n\t\t\\dfrac {18x} {y}&\t\t\n\t}\n$$\n\nNote that in the final step, we canceled out a common factor of $x$ in the numerator and denominator.",
